<%# The site's two typefaces, in one place because three layouts need them.

    The reference sets Calibre, which is licensed, so the page carries Figtree:
    the closest free face, with the same double-storey a, single-storey g and
    high x-height. IBM Plex Mono is not a substitution — it is the mono
    rubyonrails.org itself loads.

    Only the weights the reference uses are requested: 400 for body, 600 for
    anything emphasised, 700 for headlines. Nothing heavier is fetched because
    nothing heavier is set.

    Loaded from Google Fonts rather than vendored: this is the docs site, not
    the registry, and an installed component must never depend on a webfont.
    display=swap means the fallback stack renders first if the request is slow
    or the reader is offline. %>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Figtree:ital,wght@0,400..700;1,400..700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&display=swap">
